<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phocas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">547–<a href="/years/610">610 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phocas was a Byzantine emperor who seized power in 602 CE after a mutiny in which the emperor Maurice was murdered. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, who had been restored to power with Maurice's help, used the murder as a pretext for war. The resulting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-sasanian-war-of-602-628">Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628</a> CE exhausted both empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phocas.jpg" alt="Phocas" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Museum · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phocas,_British_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The proximate trigger was the Byzantine-Sasanian War of 602–628 CE, launched after the emperor Maurice, who had helped restore Khosrow II to power against the usurper Bahram Chobin in 591 CE, was overthrown and murdered by the junior officer <b>Phocas</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>According to John the Lydian, the praetorian prefect <b>Phocas</b> funded the first work with 4,000 Roman pounds of gold.</blockquote><a href="/work/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia · How It Was Made</a></li><li><blockquote>Theodosius was deposed in a military revolt and was said to have been executed by <b>Phocas</b>'s supporters.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-26">26 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Phocas</b>, leader of the army mutiny that had overthrown Emperor Maurice, had Maurice's five sons executed and then Maurice himself.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-27">27 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The fleet of Heraclius the Younger, who with his father, the Exarch of Africa, had rebelled against Emperor <b>Phocas</b> in 608, reached Constantinople.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-3">3 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Having reached Constantinople on 3 October at the head of the revolt against the unpopular emperor <b>Phocas</b>, Heraclius was crowned in the Chapel of St Stephen within the Great Palace.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-5">5 October in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=42,26&amp;year=587" aria-label="Thrace on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5182 668 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Phocas"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5632 938h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5632 938h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=42,26&amp;year=587">What was here in 587 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
